# armour/woman/plate: steel plate cut to the woman's torso (P2c slice, SLICE-ARMOUR; STYLE_P2 25.3): the same plates as
# the man's, the breastplate shaped by ONE step-1 row across the chest under the bust (never sculpted cups), the waist a
# pixel narrower than the man's (the tunic's waist column erased under it), the fauld lames over her hips. The sleeve caps
# of her torso (facing down and up) are steel; the pauldrons are shared (shared/pauldron_plate_*), her tassets plate_hang.
# Keys: rest idle run runl drawn swing lie in D U R L (side runl: the method's lean rows; the L lie is the rest).
# Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
use person
body woman
role armour plate
layer torso
anchor neck
keys torso
z 2

